Color [SimTalk] - Connector
Sets the color of the Connector designated by <Connector-Path>.
Remarks
Set the RGB values of the color with the method makeRGBValue. If you assign an invalid value to the
attribute Color, Plant Simulation retains the current color.
The Connectors in 3D use the color you define here as well. The default RGB color 7, 0, 0 of the Connector
in Plant Simulation is interpreted as white in 3D. All other colors are applied as you define them in Plant
Simulation.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Connector-Path>.Color:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyStation.succConnector(3).Color := makeRGBValue(100,100,100)
MyStation.succConnector(3).Color := 6579300 // is the same as the color 
above
SimTalk
makeRGBValue [SimTalk]
See also
Color [Connector]
